        // Page Content
        .container-fluid.p-0

            // About
            section#about.resume-section
                .resume-section-content
                    h1.mb-0
                        | Greg  
                        span.text-primary Hemmes
                    .subheading.mb-5
                        | Louisville, KY  
                        //- a(href='greghemmes@outlook.com') greghemmes@outlook.com
                    p.lead.mb-5
                        |  Data center engineer specializing in physical infrastructure, structured cabling, and critical facility operations across enterprise and government environments. Experienced in rack design, hardware lifecycle management, and BMS/PLC systems, with a strong foundation in networking, IT systems and cybersecurity.
                    .social-icons
                        a.social-icon(href='mailto:greghemmes@outlook.com')
                            i.far.fa-envelope
                        a.social-icon(href='https://www.linkedin.com/in/gregory-hemmes/')
                            i.fab.fa-linkedin-in
                        a.social-icon(href='https://github.com/ghemmes')
                            i.fab.fa-github


            hr.m-0

            // Experience
            section#experience.resume-section
               .resume-section-content
                    h2.mb-5 Experience

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Data Center Engineer
                            .subheading.mb-3 Commonwealth Office of Technology
                            ul
                                li  Plan rack layouts and manage customers and contractors to meet power, space, and infrastructure requirements.
                                li  Monitor network and infrastructure platforms to detect, escalate, and resolve incidents before service impact.
                                li  Troubleshoot and maintain BMS and PLC logic controllers across critical mechanical infrastructure.
                                li  Install, terminate, test, and troubleshoot copper and fiber cabling across IDF/MDF and data center environments.
                                li  Manage hardware lifecycle and standardize cabling, labeling, and rack design to improve accuracy and consistency.

                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary Frankfort, KY &nbsp; | &nbsp;  August 2025 - Present

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Data Center Technician
                            a.subheading.mb-3(href='http://www.humana.com/') Humana
                            ul
                                li  Deployed, configured, and audited enterprise hardware to maintain high availability and operational reliability.
                                li  Upgraded enterprise server components to meet performance and capacity requirements.
                                li  Responded to incidents via bridge calls and root cause analysis, ensuring clear communication and documentation.
                                li  Supported large infrastructure upgrades, cable migrations, and rack deployments, coordinating with vendors, field engineers, and internal teams to minimize downtime.

                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary Louisville, KY &nbsp; | &nbsp;  July 2024 - July 2025
         
                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Desktop/End User Support Tech 3
                            a.subheading.mb-3(href='http://www.humana.com/') Humana
                            ul
                                li  Served on the escalation team resolving software, hardware, networking, and application issues for global users.
                                li  Developed PowerShell scripts to automate device health checks and software installations, improving efficiency.
                                li  Managed incident resolutions, ensuring communication, documentation, and smooth handoffs between teams.

                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary Louisville, KY &nbsp; | &nbsp;  May 2023 - July 2024

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Network Specialist
                            a.subheading.mb-3(href='http://www.itgcorporation.com/') Integrated Technology Group
                            ul
                                li  Resolved network and access issues while supporting core network operations and policy management.
                                li  Led a company-wide audit and remediation to identify and bring unmanaged devices into compliance.
                                li  Automated patching and maintenance using remote monitoring tools, improving endpoint visibility and security.

                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary East Greenbush, NY &nbsp; | &nbsp;  January 2022 - May 2023

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Mobile App Developer (Freelance)
                            a.subheading.mb-3(href='http://www.lawnadmin.com') LawnAdmin
                            ul
                                li  Co-developed a full-stack mobile app for scheduling, customer management, and invoicing.
                                li  Worked directly with clients to gather requirements, prioritize features, and provide ongoing post-launch support.
                                li  Created a promotional website to improve the business’s online presence and drive customer engagement.
                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary Albany, NY &nbsp; | &nbsp;  October 2020 - January 2025

